      "message": "Now the pkvm will update the hvcpu-\u003earch.xcr0 and hvcpu-\u003earch.ia32_xss if host changes them. And my understanding about the purpose of pkvm_restore_host_xsave_state is to restore the xcr0 and MSR_IA32_XSS to the trusted fixed value other than re-using the value set by the host, e.g, not to reuse the value saved in hvcpu-\u003earch.xcr0 and hvcpu-\u003earch.ia32_xss.\n\nThen seems we don\u0027t need to overwrite hvcpu-\u003earch.xcr0 and hvcpu-\u003earch.ia32_xss with kvm_host\u0027s value, instead we need to restore xcr0 and MSR_IA32_XSS with the hvcpu-\u003earch.xcr0 and hvcpu-\u003earch.ia32_xss before switch back to the host, to make the host see consistent values it sets? Or maybe I misunderstood something?",
